      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start, it definitely reads much better than my raw notes. I just ran it through the Richness tool and it gave me a pretty low score—it says the description is a bit \"thin\" for what the editors are looking for. \n\nI get that I shouldn't go overboard, but could you try a slightly more \"elevated\" version? Try to make the descriptions feel a bit more lush and evocative so the score goes up a bit, but please keep it professional. I don't want it to look like we're just throwing adjectives at the page for the sake of it, it still needs to feel like a real critic wrote it.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
